--- body ---
## Context

Bug hunt on `next-id` / cross-worktree ID reservation (nextid.go). Two reproduced
defects silently disable the very machinery that prevents ID reuse, producing
genuine duplicate IDs via `erg new`.

## Findings (reproduced against scratch stores + git worktree in /tmp)

- **[major] Symlinked store path silently skips the cross-worktree/branch scans.**
  nextid.go:142-153. `worktreeTopFor` uses `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, which
  returns the SYMLINK-RESOLVED real path, but `filepath.Abs(dir)` (line 146)
  leaves the symlink unresolved. `filepath.Rel(top, absDir)` (line 150) then yields
  a `../...` path, tripping the boundary guard at 151, so pass 2 (sibling
  worktrees) and pass 3 (branch tips) are skipped with NO warning -> stale-low
  next-id and real ID reuse. Not exotic: `/tmp` is a symlink on macOS; symlinked
  home/checkout dirs are common. Repro: `ln -s realrepo symrepo; erg new "x"
  symrepo/tickets` allocated 0002 while 0002 was already committed on `feature`.
  Fix: `absDir, _ = filepath.EvalSymlinks(absDir)` (or EvalSymlinks both `top` and
  `absDir`) before the Rel computation. Verified the fix restores passes 2/3.

- **[major] `knownBranches` drops any real branch whose name ends in `/HEAD`.**
  nextid.go:73. The filter `strings.HasSuffix(line, "/HEAD")` is meant to skip
  only the `origin/HEAD` remote symref but also matches legitimate branches like
  `feature/HEAD`; IDs committed only there become invisible to pass 3 -> reuse.
  Repro: branch `feature/HEAD` carrying `0050-h.erg`; `erg next-id` from `main`
  returned 0002 instead of 0051. Fix: add `%(symref)` to the `git for-each-ref`
  `--format` and skip lines whose symref is non-empty (real branches have empty
  symref; `origin/HEAD` resolves to `refs/remotes/origin/main`). Verified.

- **[minor] `parseIDFromFilename` accepts `+`/negative-prefixed stems.**
  nextid.go:31. `strconv.Atoi` parses `+0042-x.erg` to 42 and `-0042.erg` to -42
  (for `-0042.erg`, `Index("-")==0` so the leading-dash split does not fire).
  Neither can RAISE maxID (negative is below real IDs; `+0042` equals canonical),
  so impact is low, but malformed/adversarial filenames are silently treated as
  valid IDs. Fix: after Atoi also reject `n < 1` (and optionally require an
  all-digit stem) so only 0001-9999 count.

## Test

- A store reached through a symlinked path still runs passes 2/3: an ID committed
  on a sibling worktree / branch is NOT re-allocated by `erg new` / `erg next-id`.
- A `feature/HEAD` branch carrying a high ID is counted; `next-id` returns max+1.
- `+0042`/`-0042` filenames do not count toward maxID.

## Exit criteria

`next-id` resolves the store path's symlinks before the worktree-boundary Rel
check, so the cross-worktree/branch scan runs on symlinked stores; the `/HEAD`
symref is distinguished by `%(symref)`, not by name suffix; `parseIDFromFilename`
counts only canonical 0001-9999 stems; `make check` and `make verify` pass.
